BT /F2 16 Tf 0.02 0.44 0.50 rg 1 0 0 1 50 713.0 Tm (DESIGN TRADE-OFFS AND HISTORICAL LIMITATIONS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (OFS reflects floppy-disk priorities: inexpensive integrity checks, native Amiga metadata) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (and explicit block ownership. Embedding 24-byte metadata headers in data blocks reduces) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (useful data per block and creates additional work during sequential reads. FFS addressed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (part of this performance limitation by storing file data without OFS-style headers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 597.0 Tm (Old AmigaDOS formats are historically significant but are not uniform across DOS0/2/4/6.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (The directory-cache variation speeds some lookups at additional maintenance cost.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (International and long-name variants need compatible name comparison and encoding policies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (Rigid assumptions about 512-byte blocks must not be used where larger blocks are permitted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (by the format.) Tj ET
